[[:db/cas 17592186110979 :question/problem "${(\\frac{-2x}{5})}^{3}=$" "${\\left(\\frac{-2x}{5}\\right)}^{3}=$"] [:db/cas 17592186110979 :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{-2x}{5})}^{3}=\\frac{(-2x)^{3}}{{5}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power of product rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(-2x)^{3}}{{5}^{3}} &= \\frac{(-2)^{3}{x}^{3}}{125} \\\\ &= -\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{125}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\left(\\frac{-2x}{5}\\right)}^{3}=\\frac{(-2x)^{3}}{{5}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power of product rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(-2x)^{3}}{{5}^{3}} &= \\frac{(-2)^{3}{x}^{3}}{125} \\\\ &= -\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{125}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186110980 :question/problem "Simplify $9(\\frac{x}{3})^{3}$." "Simplify $9\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)^{3}$."] [:db/cas 17592186493893 :question/problem "${(\\frac{3wt}{8})}^{2}=$" "${\\left(\\frac{3wt}{8}\\right)}^{2}=$"] [:db/cas 17592186493893 :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{3wt}{8})}^{2}=\\frac{(3wt)^{2}}{{8}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(3wt)^{2}}{{8}^{2}} &= \\frac{{3}^{2}{w}^{2}{t}^{2}}{{8}^{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{9{w}^{2}{t}^{2}}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\left(\\frac{3wt}{8}\\right)}^{2}=\\frac{(3wt)^{2}}{{8}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(3wt)^{2}}{{8}^{2}} &= \\frac{{3}^{2}{w}^{2}{t}^{2}}{{8}^{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{9{w}^{2}{t}^{2}}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186493897 :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${(\\frac{wt}{2})}^{4}?$" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\left(\\frac{wt}{2}\\right)}^{4}?$"] [:db/cas 17592186493897 :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{wt}{2})}^{4}=\\frac{(wt)^{4}}{{2}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(wt)^{4}}{{2}^{4}}=\\frac{{w}^{4}{t}^{4}}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\left(\\frac{wt}{2}\\right)}^{4}=\\frac{(wt)^{4}}{{2}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(wt)^{4}}{{2}^{4}}=\\frac{{w}^{4}{t}^{4}}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186553590 :question/problem "${(\\frac{3}{2})}^{4}=$" "${\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}^{4}=$"] [:db/cas 17592186553590 :question/worked-solution "We apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{4}=\\frac{{3}^{4}}{{2}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}^{4}=\\frac{{3}^{4}}{{2}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186558498 :question/problem "Simplify $6{(\\frac{2a}{3})}^{3}.$" "Simplify $6{\\left(\\frac{2a}{3}\\right)}^{3}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186558498 :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{(\\frac{2a}{3})}^{3}=6\\cdot \\frac{(2a)^{3}}{{3}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power of product rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\cdot \\frac{(2a)^{3}}{{3}^{3}} &= 6\\cdot \\frac{{2}^{3}{a}^{3}}{{3}^{3}} \\\\ &= 6\\cdot \\frac{8{a}^{3}}{27} \\\\ &= \\frac{48{a}^{3}}{27} \\\\ &= \\frac{16{a}^{3}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{\\left(\\frac{2a}{3}\\right)}^{3}=6\\cdot \\frac{(2a)^{3}}{{3}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power of product rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\cdot \\frac{(2a)^{3}}{{3}^{3}} &= 6\\cdot \\frac{{2}^{3}{a}^{3}}{{3}^{3}} \\\\ &= 6\\cdot \\frac{8{a}^{3}}{27} \\\\ &= \\frac{48{a}^{3}}{27} \\\\ &= \\frac{16{a}^{3}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186110297 :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{2x}{3})}^{4}=\\frac{(2x)^{4}}{{3}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(2x)^{4}}{{3}^{4}} &= \\frac{{2}^{4}{x}^{4}}{{3}^{4}} \\\\ &= \\frac{16{x}^{4}}{81}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\left(\\frac{2x}{3}\\right)}^{4}=\\frac{(2x)^{4}}{{3}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(2x)^{4}}{{3}^{4}} &= \\frac{{2}^{4}{x}^{4}}{{3}^{4}} \\\\ &= \\frac{16{x}^{4}}{81}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186110981 :question/problem "What is $\\frac{4}{3}(\\frac{v}{4})^{2}(\\frac{3}{u})^{2}$?" "What is $\\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\frac{v}{4}\\right)^{2}\\left(\\frac{3}{u}\\right)^{2}$?"] [:db/cas 17592186111332 :question/problem "What is $(\\frac{2x}{3})^{2}(\\frac{3}{x})^{3}$?" "What is $\\left(\\frac{2x}{3}\\right)^{2}\\left(\\frac{3}{x}\\right)^{3}$?"] [:db/cas 17592186493895 :question/problem "${(\\frac{s}{2})}^{4}{(\\frac{4}{t})}^{2}=$" "${\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right)}^{4}{\\left(\\frac{4}{t}\\right)}^{2}=$"] [:db/cas 17592186493895 :question/worked-solution "We apply the power of quotient rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{s}{2})}^{4}{(\\frac{4}{t})}^{2} &= \\frac{{s}^{4}}{{2}^{4}}\\cdot \\frac{{4}^{2}}{{t}^{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{{s}^{4}}{16}\\cdot \\frac{16}{{t}^{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{16{s}^{4}}{16{t}^{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{{s}^{4}}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We apply the power of quotient rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right)}^{4}{\\left(\\frac{4}{t}\\right)}^{2} &= \\frac{{s}^{4}}{{2}^{4}}\\cdot \\frac{{4}^{2}}{{t}^{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{{s}^{4}}{16}\\cdot \\frac{16}{{t}^{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{16{s}^{4}}{16{t}^{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{{s}^{4}}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186493905 :question/problem "${(\\frac{3}{4x})}^{2}{(\\frac{-2x}{5})}^{3}=$" "${\\left(\\frac{3}{4x}\\right)}^{2}{\\left(\\frac{-2x}{5}\\right)}^{3}=$"] [:db/cas 17592186493905 :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{3}{4x})}^{2}{(\\frac{-2x}{5})}^{3}=\\frac{{3}^{2}}{(4x)^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{(-2x)^{3}}{{5}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we apply the power of product rule and multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{3}^{2}}{(4x)^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{(-2x)^{3}}{{5}^{3}} &= \\frac{{3}^{2}}{{4}^{2}{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{(-2)^{3}{x}^{3}}{{5}^{3}} \\\\ &= \\frac{9}{16{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{-8{x}^{3}}{125} \\\\ &= \\frac{-8\\cdot 9{x}^{3}}{16\\cdot 125{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we apply the quotient rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-8\\cdot 9{x}^{3}}{16\\cdot 125{x}^{2}} &= -\\frac{9{x}^{3-2}}{2\\cdot 125} \\\\ &= -\\frac{9x}{250}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\left(\\frac{3}{4x}\\right)}^{2}{\\left(\\frac{-2x}{5}\\right)}^{3}=\\frac{{3}^{2}}{(4x)^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{(-2x)^{3}}{{5}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we apply the power of product rule and multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{3}^{2}}{(4x)^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{(-2x)^{3}}{{5}^{3}} &= \\frac{{3}^{2}}{{4}^{2}{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{(-2)^{3}{x}^{3}}{{5}^{3}} \\\\ &= \\frac{9}{16{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{-8{x}^{3}}{125} \\\\ &= \\frac{-8\\cdot 9{x}^{3}}{16\\cdot 125{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we apply the quotient rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-8\\cdot 9{x}^{3}}{16\\cdot 125{x}^{2}} &= -\\frac{9{x}^{3-2}}{2\\cdot 125} \\\\ &= -\\frac{9x}{250}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186493913 :question/problem "${(-\\frac{a}{b})}^{3}{(\\frac{c}{d})}^{2}=$" "${\\left(-\\frac{a}{b}\\right)}^{3}{\\left(\\frac{c}{d}\\right)}^{2}=$"] [:db/cas 17592186493913 :question/worked-solution "We apply the power of quotient rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(-\\frac{a}{b})}^{3}{(\\frac{c}{d})}^{2} &= \\frac{(-a)^{3}}{{b}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{{c}^{2}}{{d}^{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{-{a}^{3}}{{b}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{{c}^{2}}{{d}^{2}} \\\\ &= -\\frac{{a}^{3}{c}^{2}}{{b}^{3}{d}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We apply the power of quotient rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\left(-\\frac{a}{b}\\right)}^{3}{\\left(\\frac{c}{d}\\right)}^{2} &= \\frac{(-a)^{3}}{{b}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{{c}^{2}}{{d}^{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{-{a}^{3}}{{b}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{{c}^{2}}{{d}^{2}} \\\\ &= -\\frac{{a}^{3}{c}^{2}}{{b}^{3}{d}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186553503 :question/problem "$\\frac{2}{3}{(\\frac{3}{v})}^{2}{(\\frac{1}{u})}^{3}=$" "$\\frac{2}{3}{\\left(\\frac{3}{v}\\right)}^{2}{\\left(\\frac{1}{u}\\right)}^{3}=$"] [:db/cas 17592186553503 :question/worked-solution "We apply the power of quotient rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}{(\\frac{3}{v})}^{2}{(\\frac{1}{u})}^{3} &= \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{{3}^{2}}{{v}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{{1}^{3}}{{u}^{3}} \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{9}{{v}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{u}^{3}} \\\\ &= \\frac{18}{3{v}^{2}{u}^{3}} \\\\ &= \\frac{6}{{v}^{2}{u}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We apply the power of quotient rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}{\\left(\\frac{3}{v}\\right)}^{2}{\\left(\\frac{1}{u}\\right)}^{3} &= \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{{3}^{2}}{{v}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{{1}^{3}}{{u}^{3}} \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{9}{{v}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{u}^{3}} \\\\ &= \\frac{18}{3{v}^{2}{u}^{3}} \\\\ &= \\frac{6}{{v}^{2}{u}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186110298 :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{y}{2})}^{3}{(\\frac{2y}{3})}^{2}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{{2}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{(2y)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{3}}{{2}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{(2y)^{2}}{{3}^{2}} &= \\frac{{y}^{3}}{8}\\cdot \\frac{{2}^{2}{y}^{2}}{9} \\\\ &= \\frac{{y}^{3}}{8}\\cdot \\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we apply the product rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{3}}{8}\\cdot \\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9} &= \\frac{4{y}^{(3+2)}}{72} \\\\ &= \\frac{4{y}^{5}}{72} \\\\ &= \\frac{{y}^{5}}{18}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\left(\\frac{y}{2}\\right)}^{3}{\\left(\\frac{2y}{3}\\right)}^{2}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{{2}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{(2y)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{3}}{{2}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{(2y)^{2}}{{3}^{2}} &= \\frac{{y}^{3}}{8}\\cdot \\frac{{2}^{2}{y}^{2}}{9} \\\\ &= \\frac{{y}^{3}}{8}\\cdot \\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we apply the product rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{3}}{8}\\cdot \\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9} &= \\frac{4{y}^{(3+2)}}{72} \\\\ &= \\frac{4{y}^{5}}{72} \\\\ &= \\frac{{y}^{5}}{18}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186111823 :tutorial/content "The **power of quotient rule** states that if we want to raise the quotient $\\dfrac{x}{y}$ to some power $n,$ we must raise the numerator and denominator to the power $n$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{x}{y}\\right)^n=\\dfrac{x^n}{y^n}\n$$\n\nFor example,\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{x}{y}\\right)^4=\\dfrac{x^4}{y^4}.\n$$\n\nTo see why the power of quotient rule is true, let's take the above example and work it out again the long way. We get the same result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{x}{y})}^{4} &= \\frac{x}{y}\\cdot \\frac{x}{y}\\cdot \\frac{x}{y}\\cdot \\frac{x}{y} \\\\ &= \\frac{x\\cdot x\\cdot x\\cdot x}{y\\cdot y\\cdot y\\cdot y} \\\\ &= \\frac{{x}^{4}}{{y}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe power of quotient rule is just a shortcut for the process above." "The **power of quotient rule** states that if we want to raise the quotient $\\dfrac{x}{y}$ to some power $n,$ we must raise the numerator and denominator to the power $n$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{x}{y}\\right)^n=\\dfrac{x^n}{y^n}\n$$\n\nFor example,\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{x}{y}\\right)^4=\\dfrac{x^4}{y^4}.\n$$\n\nTo see why the power of quotient rule is true, let's take the above example and work it out again the long way. We get the same result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right)}^{4} &= \\frac{x}{y}\\cdot \\frac{x}{y}\\cdot \\frac{x}{y}\\cdot \\frac{x}{y} \\\\ &= \\frac{x\\cdot x\\cdot x\\cdot x}{y\\cdot y\\cdot y\\cdot y} \\\\ &= \\frac{{x}^{4}}{{y}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe power of quotient rule is just a shortcut for the process above."] [:db/ensure 17592186110297 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186110298 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186110979 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186110980 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186110981 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186111332 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186111823 :tutorial/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186493893 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186493895 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186493897 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186493905 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186493913 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186553503 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186553590 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186558498 :question/validate]]
